Ih99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AC8 mutation check — the confirmation guard is genuinely exercised (RED/GREEN recorded)\n\nRun in worktree ../despotic-s3 against the landed tree (commit 4010da6493), worktree venv.\n\nMUTATION: deleted the entire confirmation guard from `_inbound_unlink_one`\n(`apply_inbound_records.py`), i.e. removed:\n\n    if confirm_store is not None and not confirm_store.is_confirmed(\n        local_id, target_local_id, relation\n    ):\n        logger.warning(...)\n        return False\n\nRED (mutation applied) —\n`pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k \"never_confirmed or vendor_type_collision or relation_scoped or idempotent\"`:\n\n    FAILED test_declines_removal_of_a_never_confirmed_link            - assert 1 == 0\n    FAILED test_confirmation_is_relation_scoped_not_pair_scoped       - assert 1 == 0\n    FAILED test_decline_is_idempotent_across_passes                   - AssertionError: assert 1 == 0\n    FAILED test_vendor_type_collision_scenario_is_protected           - assert 1 == 0\n    4 failed, 6 deselected in 4.24s\n\nNote AC1 (`test_declines_removal_of_a_never_confirmed_link`) and AC3\n(`test_vendor_type_collision_scenario_is_protected`, the epic's motivating scenario) are both\namong the kills, which is what AC8 asks for; two further cells also detect the mutation.\n\nGREEN (mutation reverted) — same file, full suite:\n\n    10 passed in 11.00s\n\nVerdict: PASS. The tests detect the DEFECT, not the diff — with the guard removed the applier\nonce again deletes a link the peer was never proven to carry.\n\n## Supporting verification (same tree)\n\n- `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` -> 2551 passed\n- `pytest` over the three directly-affected suites post-rebase -> 50 passed\n- `make lint` exit 0; `make typecheck` -> Success, 518 source files\n- `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` -> active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0\n- all six `scripts/gen_*.py` generators re-run -> no diff (no doc/registry drift)\n- `apply_inbound_records.py` = 797 lines, under the 800 hard cap (comments condensed rather\n  than splitting the module; the split is tracked separately)\n\n## Regression fixtures (AC10 context)\n\nFive pre-existing cells began failing for the CORRECT reason — they exercise removal\nconvergence with no peer-confirmation record, which is exactly the behavior this story\nchanges. Each models a peer that HELD a link and then deleted it, which by construction\nimplies the link was synchronized, so each was given confirmation evidence rather than a\nworkaround:\n\n- `test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` (4 cells) via a `_confirm_local_deps` helper that seeds\n  from the ticket's CURRENT deps, so it stays correct for both the single-relation cells and\n  the e39f double-related pair.\n- `test_impossible_links_cicada.py::test_removals_and_healthy_adds_are_untouched` — whose\n  docstring already named this boundary (\"Guards the boundary with epic a4bd (inbound REMOVAL\n  discrimination), which owns `_inbound_unlink_one`\").\n\nBoth suites are green: 21 passed (2b16) and 19 passed (cicada).","timestamp":1786604570594923001}],"created_at":1786558530994179001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"da225617-9c9d-46ff-ac33-39b1730fa419","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"83d3-61d9-fc59-424b"},{"link_uuid":"48fcae92-c904-4e0a-bbff-6a39404b801d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f6e9-a5fd-e908-4b82"},{"link_uuid":"39ad456c-a11c-4207-8899-d9aa8972aec3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dc31-91f9-c66c-4ae8"}],"description":"## Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb`. This is the behavior-changing story the epic exists for, and\nit lands LAST: it consumes the store from S1 (`248f-ac00-18db-4259`), the snapshot evidence from\nS2 (`83d3-61d9-fc59-424b`), and — critically — the upgrade backfill from S4\n(`f6e9-a5fd-e908-4b82`), without which the first post-upgrade pass would decline every legitimate\nremoval.\n\nThe defect: `managed_refs` is monotonic and marks a ref managed the instant it is created\nLOCALLY, so guard G3 (`inbound_differ.py::_diff_link_removals_inbound`) cannot distinguish a\nnever-pushed local link from a peer-deleted one. G4 (the same-pass outbound-ADD suppression in\n`compute_inbound_mutations`) covers that blind spot ONLY when the outbound differ emits the\nre-ADD — but `outbound_links.py::_diff_links` dedups ADDs direction-agnostically on\n`(vendor_type, target_key)` and is \"intentionally NOT deduped on relation\", so a local link whose\nvendor type collides with an existing remote link in the OTHER direction (local `blocks` against\nan inward `Blocks`, which reads as `depends_on`) is never pushed AND never G4-protected. Its\nremoval record reaches the applier, and since e39f made removal relation-scoped it removes that\nnever-pushed local link.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `peer_confirmations.py` — add `open_store_or_none(repo_root)`, mirroring\n  `apply_inbound_records._open_impossible_link_store`: returns the store, or `None` when it\n  cannot be opened. The helper lives in the new module, NOT in `apply_inbound_records.py`, which\n  has under 50 lines of headroom against the 800-line cap.\n- `apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_update_apply_links` — open the confirmation store ONCE per\n  pass beside the existing `skip_store = _open_impossible_link_store(repo_root)`, and thread it\n  into `_inbound_unlink_one`. Never re-open per record.\n- `apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_unlink_one` — gains the store parameter. Before removing,\n  consult `is_confirmed(local_id, target_local_id, relation)`. If NOT confirmed: log a WARNING\n  naming the three key parts and the reason, and `return False` without writing. The return\n  value is load-bearing — `False` keeps the silent-no-op canary in `apply_handlers.py` truthful.\n- **Fail-open:** a `None` store (unopenable) disables the check entirely and restores exactly\n  today's behavior — the record is an optimisation of safety, never a precondition for applying\n  a removal. This mirrors the impossible-link store's stated contract.\n- Existing e39f behavior is preserved unchanged for confirmed links: removal stays\n  relation-scoped via `rebar.unlink(..., relation, ...)`, and a relation with no net-active local\n  link stays a logged INFO no-op.\n- Report the per-pass decline count in the existing `_inbound_update_apply_links` INFO summary\n  that already reports impossible-link skips, so declines are operator-visible rather than\n  log-only.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1 A removal record for a managed link with NO confirmation is declined: no UNLINK event\n      is written, the link is still net-active locally, a WARNING is logged, and\n      `_inbound_unlink_one` returns False. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k declines`.\n- [x] AC2 A removal record for a link WITH a confirmation still converges — the link is removed,\n      exactly the named relation and no other. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k converges`.\n- [x] AC3 The epic's motivating scenario end-to-end: a local `blocks` dep whose outbound ADD is\n      deduped by an inward same-vendor-type remote link is NOT removed by an inbound removal\n      record. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k vendor_collision`.\n- [x] AC4 Re-applying the same declined record on a later pass declines again idempotently and\n      writes nothing. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k idempotent`.\n- [x] AC5 A link whose ONLY confirmation record has `source=\"backfill\"` is REMOVED by a matching\n      removal record rather than declined — so the first post-upgrade pass declines no legitimate\n      removal. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k backfill`.\n- [x] AC6 A `None` (unopenable) store declines nothing — removal behaves exactly as before this\n      story. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k fail_open`.\n- [x] AC7 The per-pass INFO summary reports the decline count. Proof:\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py -k summary`.\n- [x] AC8 Mutation check: deleting the confirmation check turns the AC1 and AC3 tests RED;\n      restoring it turns them GREEN. Recorded as a ticket comment with both outputs.\n- [x] AC9 `apply_inbound_records.py` stays under the 800-line cap. Proof: `bash -c 'git archive\n      HEAD | tar -xO src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py | wc -l'` < 800.\n- [x] AC10 Gates green and no regression. Proof: `make lint` exit 0, `make typecheck` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` exit 0,\n      `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` exit 0.\n\n## Testing\n\n- New suite `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py`.\n  Tests are BEHAVIORAL, driven through `compute_inbound_mutations` and\n  `_inbound_update_apply_links`, matching the existing 2b16 suite's stated discipline of driving\n  public entry points and never a private helper by name.\n- Regression: the existing `test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py` suite and\n  `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_impossible_links_cicada.py` must stay green. Their\n  removal cells model a peer that HELD a link and then deleted it — which by construction implies\n  it was synchronized — so they need peer-confirmation fixtures, which is expected and must be\n  added rather than worked around.\n- Full command set: `make lint && make typecheck && pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nG3 and G4 themselves are unchanged — the discrimination is added at the applier (G5), where the\nepic's acceptance criteria place it. No change to `managed_refs` monotonicity. No change to the\noutbound ADD dedup key.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py","reason":"open_store_or_none fail-open opener"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"decline unconfirmed removals in _inbound_unlink_one; open the store once per pass; decline count in the pass summary"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py","reason":"NEW: behavioral decline/converge tests through _inbound_update_apply_links"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py","reason":"four end-to-end removal cells need peer-confirmation fixtures now that removal requires evidence"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_impossible_links_cicada.py","reason":"its removal-branch guard needs the same confirmation fixture (boundary its docstring already names)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","83d3-61d9-fc59-424b"],["depends_on","f6e9-a5fd-e908-4b82"],["parent","a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb"],["relates_to","dc31-91f9-c66c-4ae8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","parent_status_uuid":"e44947e3-0aee-4bdc-b493-3f2b3532c46c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"47a0-7019-da4b-40e0","ticket_type":"story","title":"Decline inbound removal of never-peer-confirmed links","v